## Naming & Clarity
- Functions: verbs. Variables: descriptive nouns. Prefer full words.
- Names should eliminate need for comments.

## Types
- Strict TypeScript. Annotate public/exported signatures.
- Avoid `any`. Use discriminated unions and narrow types explicitly.

## Control Flow
- Guard clauses first. Handle edge cases early. Avoid deep nesting.
- Never catch and ignore errors. Surface actionable messages with context.

## Async & Streaming
- Pass `AbortSignal` through handlers/services.
- Support streaming with backpressure-friendly APIs.

## Validation
- Validate external inputs early (use `zod` where appropriate).
- Convert to internal types in handlers. Sanitize user content.

## Documentation
- JSDoc (`/** ... */`) for public APIs.
- Document intent (why), not mechanics (how), unless non-obvious.

## Formatting
- Prettier is source of truth. Match existing style. Avoid unrelated reformatting.

## Centralized Utilities
- Error types in `src/errors/**`
- Pure helpers in `src/utils/**`

@src/errors/**
@src/utils/**
